From c116613a7f9c1cbbcdd91c83f404c9cf5ff282d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel McDonough <90170351+daniel-mcdonough@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:05:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH pyra-meta] pyra-meta-mate: depend on mate-polkit before
 network-manager-gnome

network-manager-gnome depends on "policykit-1-gnome | polkit-1-auth-agent".
policykit-1-gnome is gone in trixie, so apt picks a polkit-1-auth-agent
provider while resolving it, before it reaches mate-polkit through
mate-desktop-environment. It takes ukui-polkit, the first provider it
finds, and the image ends up with both agents.

ukui-polkit's autostart entry includes MATE and puts the agent in
mate-session's Initialization phase, but the agent never registers with
the session manager. mate-session waits for it until its phase timeout,
so every login sits about 30 seconds before the window manager starts:

  WARNING: Application 'polkit-ukui-authentication-agent-1.desktop'
  failed to register before timeout

Naming mate-polkit ahead of network-manager-gnome makes apt mark it
first, and nm-applet's dependency is then already satisfied. Simulated
with apt-get install -s on trixie armhf: as shipped, both agents are
installed; with this change, only mate-polkit. Listing mate-polkit after
network-manager-gnome does not help.

Measured on a Pyra on Debian 13: the panel appears about 7 seconds after
the password instead of about 35.
---
 debian/control | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/debian/control b/debian/control
index 217ca58..c8bd776 100644
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -89,9 +89,9 @@ Description: Xfce desktop for pyra (metapackage)
 
 Package: pyra-meta-mate
 Architecture: all
-Depends: ${misc:Depends}, pyra-meta-desktop-base, caja-open-terminal,
- network-manager-gnome, modem-manager-gui, mate-desktop-environment,
- lightdm, pyra-meta-extra
+Depends: ${misc:Depends}, pyra-meta-desktop-base, mate-polkit,
+ caja-open-terminal, network-manager-gnome, modem-manager-gui,
+ mate-desktop-environment, lightdm, pyra-meta-extra
 Description: Mate desktop for pyra (metapackage)
  The Pyra will be a perfect pocket device for everyday computing,
  gaming, emulation or hacking. It is a unique combination of a gaming
